        "original_id": "5162a57f-3bcb-59f6-8075-957ef2aaf21f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Al-Karaji, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nahawandi\n- Roles: Mathematician, engineer, astronomer\n- Places: Baghdad\n- Topics: Persian scholars in medieval science\n\nFacts:\n- Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nahawandi was a Persian astronomer of the 8th and 9th centuries.\n- Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn al Ḥusayn al-Karajī lived circa 953 to circa 1029.\n- Al-Karaji was a 10th-century Persian mathematician and engineer.\n- Al-Karaji flourished at Baghdad.",
